      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-01-27_WidnesExaminer_art0045" n="art0045">
        <head>INTERNATIONAL MATCHES.</head>
        <p>INTERNATIONAL MATCHES.</p>
        <p>G. T. P. G. T. r. England 1 1 8 Wales 0 0 0 At Twickenham. Scotland At Inverleith. COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP.</p>
        <p>Northumberland... 3 427 Durham "' 1 11 At Gateshead. THE AUSTRALASIANS AT BARROW.</p>
        <p>At Cavendish Park, Barrow, before 1,000 spectators, the smallness of the " gate" being chiefly attributable to the Northern Union commanding a shilling admission to the ground. The pace of the tourists g2nerally placed the homesters at a disadvantage, but there were many keen movements which showed Barrow in a better light than on the occasion of the first encounter. Playing with a strong wind behind them, BMWw were early aggressive, and from a good position Treloar dropped a goal. Frew ley and Gilbert led the tourists, and a transfer from Ballet enabled Berecry to run round Treloar and Morgan and score near touch. Craig failed at goal. Hallett and Berecry were again prominent, and the first named scored, Craig again missing the goal. Hiokton registered an unimproved try for Barrow, who had Hailes removed off the field injured. Interval— Australasians 6 points, Barrow 5 points. The second half went in favour of the visitors. Hallett, Gilbert, Berecry, and Frawley each scored, and Francis landed two goals from four attempts. Frawley worked hard for his score, and he maintained his record of having registered a try in each naatch in which he has played with the Colonials. Result : Australasians 2 goals and 6 tries (22 points), Barrow 1 goal and 1 try (5 points).</p>
      </div>
