      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-01-27_WidnesExaminer_art0098" n="art0098">
        <head>Borough Police Court.</head>
        <p>Borough Police Court.</p>
        <p>TCESDA Y.—Before Councillor El Roberts (in the chair), Messrs J Rymer Young and T Locker. 'Dr srr OF COKN.—WiII lam Lowe, 233, Winwick-road, was charged with felioniously stealing on January 15th two bags of coke, valued at is., the property of the Warrington Corporation. The Chief Constable said that prisoner was in the employ of Harry Challinor, a coal carrier for the Corporation. On Monday week last, the prisoner was ordered to take a load of coke from the works at Longford to Our Lady's School, Latchford. He took the coke to that address and the caretaker noticed that when he was going away he had five bags of coke on the lurry. She asked the prisoner why they were there and he said he had to take them to Orford-lane. Subsequently she went into the cellar and found there was a shortage of coke, and during the week she found the coke was being used up faster than usual. She,therefore, informed Mr. Challinor who knew the man should have left all the coke at the school. Oa enquiries being made it was found that prisoner had taken two sacks to hiS home after having tried to sell them in the St. Marr street district. —Prisoner, who pleaded guilty, was; committed to prison for one mouth with hard labour. TIIITR';DAY.—Before Messrs. J. Rymer Young (in the chair), W. Roberts, A. J. Jolley, C. Jackson Holmes, W. T. Williams, J. Upson and Dr. Naden. A WOMAN ,1N TROUIILE.—Annie Callagan, of no fixed address was charged with stealing on the 21th inst., two pairs of boots and four pairs of stockings, value 2s. J. from 99, Mersey-street. The case was adjourned until Tuesday for further inquiries to be made.</p>
