      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-01-27_WidnesExaminer_art0138" n="art0138">
        <head>LOCAL FRIENDLY SOCIETIES.</head>
        <p>LOCAL FRIENDLY SOCIETIES.</p>
        <p>Oddfellowshlp:</p>
        <p>The annual meeticg ef the Navigation Lodge (Warrington District M. Unity 1.0.0. F ) Cadishead 724 was held in the Wesleyan Schools, Lord-street, as the Lodge room has been found too small for the attendance of its members. Over 200 members were present. J. Grant P.G. presided and was supported by the Trustees and the Lodge Officers, also Bros. Bighorn and D.G.M. and F. Webster,C.S. of the District The balance sheet showed another very satisfactory year for 1911. After paying £258 4s. 4d. in sick claims £132 us. 7d. to the district, funeral, sick and manage-, Funds, writing off £3O as depreciation to building fund, the sum of £144 9s 7d. was added to the funds, making the total funds of the Lodge £2,868 Bs. Id. with a membership of 377. This Lodge is making good progress, the increase of funds for ten years being £1,324 17s. 10d. The increase of members for ten years is 01. The sick pay for ten years £2,230 175., death claims £515. After the business of the year had been disposed of the Insurance Bill was discussed. Bro. Webster explained the main points, but as the Board of Directors have called for a conference to be held in London at the end of this month nothing very definite can be artived at, but with the resources of this Lodge, it is expected something beneficial will be done for the present members. It was with regret the Lodge had to receive the resignation of its treasurer, Peter Barrow, PG., after many years good work. The Lancashire and Yorkshire Bank was appointed to be the Lodge Treasurer for the time being. Votes of thanks to the Auditors and Chairman for presiding were passed and suitably replied to. Order of Druids. The usual monthly meeting of the "Lord Elliot Lodge was held at the "Unicorn," Winwick-road, on Saturday, when the opportunity was taken of present- ing a beautful gold medallion of the Order, suitably inscribed, to Bro William Gill (late secretary), in recognition of valuable services rendered to the members for a period of over 21 years. Bro. Gill was also the recipient, on behalf of his wife, of a handsome gold brooch.— Bro J Carr, N.GA , who presided, made the presentations, and in an interesting speech spoke in felicitous terms of Bro Gill's useful work, and said he had been actuated by the best possible movements in carrying out his arduous duties. They hoped the gifts would link him more closely to his brotherhood. Bros J ft Palmer (Lodge secretary), J Blackwood (treasurer), P.N GA. Charles Massey and P.N.G.A</p>
