        <p>Part songs nicely given by the choir added to the pleasure of the evening. On Thursday and Friday even- inf.s, a similar programme was carried out, the soloists being Miss Greta Welford, of West Kirby, and Mr I Willett, of Warrington. Mr Brymer was the elecution- ist. The accompanist being Mr H Champ.</p>
        <p>BILLIARDS. WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT LEAGUE. OUR LADY'S V. CATHOLIC Y.M.S.—Mtich interest was centred in a billiard match between Our Lady's team and the C.Y.M.S. on Friday evening last. The results were : OUR LADY'S. C.Y.M'S. C McDonald Rev Father Conroy lOO P Delaney S Millington B3 M Cunningham lOO C Turner lOO P Cunningham 77 S H Smith lOO 0 Toole J Corcoran 42 D Shepherd G T Bibby T H Ridgway lOO E Toole 64 661 619 Our Lady's won by the narrow majority of 12. LIBERAL CLUB V. RYLANDS.—At Bewsey-street. Scores : LIBERAL CLUB. RYLANDS. F Mullery S Woods lOO 1 Sinclair E Sanders W Ford W Woods H Littlewood C Jordan 9O R Hamblett W Patrick lOO G Langley 5B 740 603 Liberals win by 137. SENIOR CONSERVATIVE CLUB V. CHURCH OP OUR LADY'S LATCHFORD.—This match took place on Monday i evening at the Sankey-street Cho and resulted in a win for the home team by 198. Mr. J. Buxton was in grand form for the Conservatives, making a break of 35, winning his game by 75. For the visitors Mr. McDonald played flue billiards, but in the end was beaten by 3. Scores : SENIOR. CHURCH OF OUR LADY. Trooper lOO 0 Turner 72 E 1 Parkes lOO C McDonald 97 R Straw 75 S H Smith lOO C H Wells T Lawrence T Horrabin R Ellis lOO T Ridgway J Buxton lOO Rigby ........ ....... 25 • 767 569 Seniors won by 193.</p>
